### Bundle M - Evaluate as a selective prediction system (COMPLETED 2026-11-03)
**Project directory:** `eval/`.

The reframing rather than another number. This pipeline already behaves as a
selective classifier: the deterministic layer settles what it can, model tiers
opine on the rest, and anything unsettled becomes `manual_review` and goes to a
person. So `manual_review` is a **deferral**, not a fourth label beside `clean`,
`spam` and `threat`, and the operative numbers are **coverage** - the share of
the queue automated with no human in the loop - and **selective risk**, the error
rate among those automated. A single-threshold accuracy hides exactly the question
an operator asks, and it also dissolved an uncomfortable measurement: "the models
changed no disposition" is a null result under accuracy and a legible statement
about the frontier under a risk-coverage curve.

