decide), and `external.model_tier` is a required block whose statement says in terms that
**the model-tier A/B has not run**. The honesty cost of the rows road is recorded rather
than smoothed: the pinned sha256 describes the repository file, the measured text came from
Hugging Face's converted Parquet, and the only comparison available between those two
objects is the split name and the row count - which agrees, split by split, with no
truncated cell. Deepset is measured with its licence disagreement intact and printed, not
settled. Phase 2 is now N8 and nothing else: run the tiers over these same wrapped
messages, record FPR at a stated threshold, and give the deterministic numbers the
baseline they were supposed to be compared against.

### Bundle S - Weight tiers by measured reliability, not by self-reported confidence  (SCOPED 2026-11-04, NOT STARTED)

Found by the full-stack live A/B, and it is the most consequential finding in docs/LIVE-AB.md.

Clearance requires every consulted tier to vote clean at or above a fixed 0.857 bar, and a
tier's confidence is its own band mapped through {"high": 0.90, "medium": 0.70, "low": 0.40}.
Two adjudicators of near-identical measured accuracy - local recall 0.800 / FPR 0.125, remote
recall 0.831 / FPR 0.145 - produced a fourteen-fold difference in auto-clearance (84 messages
against 6 of 1,327) and inverted the error profile: the local arm made 8 false clearances and
1 false accusation, the remote arm 1 and 6. Aggregate selective risk was the same, 5.2% against
4.8%. The difference is how each model phrases certainty, not how often it is right.

Observed directly on one benign business email: fast tiers alone (classifier clean 1.00,
injection clean 0.98) dispositioned CLEAN at 0.98; adding an adjudicator that voted clean at
0.40 dispositioned the same message manual_review, "the consulted tiers agree on clean but are
not confident enough to act on it". A low-confidence agreement blocks clearance while confident
agreement from tiers measured at 0.254 and 0.470 false-positive rate produces one. The rule
rewards overconfidence.

It also reframes an earlier headline: the 84.2% coverage at zero risk on 203 real benign
business emails came from the fast tiers alone under that rule, which is the same mechanism
that produced 437 false accusations on the benign Bengali set. That corpus was in-domain, so
it happened to be right; nothing in the mechanism is what made it right.

Shape of the fix: now that per-tier recall and false-positive rate are measured and recorded,
weight a tier's contribution by measured reliability rather than by its band, or calibrate each
model's bands against a held-out split before letting them gate a clearance. Either is a change
to core adjudication and will move the committed synthetic and adversarial numbers, which is
why it was scoped and not attempted thirteen hours before a deadline. Bundle R (symmetry for
accusation) and this one should be designed together: both are the same complaint, that the
adjudication rule does not use what measurement now knows.


### Bundle R - Require a verified finding before an accusation  (SCOPED 2026-11-03, NOT STARTED)

Found by the live model-tier A/B, not by inspection. The clearance veto stops a model from
wrongly CLEARING a threat, and nothing symmetric stops a model from wrongly ACCUSING, because
on a message the deterministic layer cannot settle there is no verified finding for a veto to
defend - so the tiers are the only voice, and out of domain they are not reliable enough to
accuse on.

Measured: deterministic-only deferred all 3,005 external messages; with live tiers the same
messages produced 1,059 accusations, 437 of them on the 840-row benign Bengali set, and 21 to
23 percent of `notinject`, which is benign by construction. On real benign business email the
same pipeline made zero false accusations, so this is a domain-shift failure and not a general
one - which is exactly why it was invisible until external corpora were measured.

Two candidate shapes, and the choice is a design decision, not an implementation detail:

1. An accusation requires at least one VERIFIED finding corroborating it, symmetric to the
   clearance veto. A message whose only adverse evidence is model opinion defers to a human.
2. Refuse to disposition mail with no authentication headers at all, deferring it, on the
   grounds that a message whose provenance cannot be checked is not a message a tier should
   accuse on.

(1) is narrower and keeps working on real mail whose auth fails legitimately; (2) is simpler
and would have deferred every external corpus row here, which makes it untestable against
this evidence. Prefer (1) and measure both.

Deliberately NOT implemented during the submission window: it changes core adjudication with
roughly sixteen hours to the deadline, and the committed synthetic and adversarial numbers are
verified as they stand. Recorded so the finding is not lost and so nobody re-derives it.

